        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-8">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 bg-white">
                    <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--primary-color);">Code of Conduct for Students & Staff</h1>
                    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
                        AGM Rural College of Engineering & Technology maintains high standards of discipline, academic integrity, and moral character. The code of conduct applies to all enrolled students, teaching faculty, and administrative staff across campus.
                    </p>

                    <hr class="my-4">

                    <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-person-check-fill text-primary me-2"></i>1. General Campus Discipline</h4>
                    <ul class="list-unstyled space-y-2 text-secondary ms-3">
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check2-circle text-success me-2"></i>Students must wear official college ID cards visibly at all times on campus.</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check2-circle text-success me-2"></i>Strict adherence to prescribed formal dress code and laboratory attire is mandatory.</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check2-circle text-success me-2"></i>Use of mobile phones inside classrooms, seminar halls, and laboratories during academic hours is strictly prohibited.</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check2-circle text-success me-2"></i>Campus cleanliness and institutional property must be maintained with utmost care.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mt-4 mb-3"><i class="bi bi-shield-x text-danger me-2"></i>2. Anti-Ragging Policy (Zero Tolerance)</h4>
                    <p class="text-muted">
                        Ragging in any form—physical, verbal, or mental—is strictly banned as per AICTE and Supreme Court directives. Any student found guilty of ragging will face immediate suspension, rustication, and police reporting.
                    </p>

                    <h4 class="fw-bold text-dark mt-4 mb-3"><i class="bi bi-journal-check text-warning me-2"></i>3. Academic Attendance & Integrity</h4>
                    <ul class="list-unstyled space-y-2 text-secondary ms-3">
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check2-circle text-success me-2"></i>Minimum 85% attendance in theory classes and 90% in practical sessions as mandated by VTU rules.</li>
                        <li class="mb-2"><i class="bi bi-check2-circle text-success me-2"></i>Plagiarism or malpractice during internal tests and semester-end examinations will result in immediate disqualification.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-4 rounded-3 d-flex align-items-center gap-3">
                        <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-pdf-fill fs-2 text-danger"></i>
                        <div>
                            <h6 class="fw-bold mb-1">Official Code of Conduct Document</h6>
                            <p class="mb-0 small">Download the official detailed AGMRCET Student & Staff HR Policy handbook.</p>
                        </div>
                        <a href="/docs/AGMRCET HR POLICY.pdf" target="_blank" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm ms-auto text-nowrap">Download PDF</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

